INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:__main__:Prompting GPT
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:
{
  "action": "Given the current environmental conditions and my agent status, I will focus on addressing my mild hunger and thirst while ensuring minimal ecological impact. My overall health is good, with high energy that allows me to be proactive in gathering resources. The environment is abundant with resources such as deer, rabbits, and berries, which provides an opportunity to sustain my needs. However, I must be mindful of my previous reflections on sustainability and the importance of not overharvesting berries.\n\nI will start by collecting water from the stream, as it is a reliable and clear source. This action will address my low thirst level without significantly altering the environment. I will ensure that my water collection technique minimizes disturbance to the natural setting, drawing on my skill in Stream-Based Water Collection.\n\nFor sustenance, I will forage for berries, as my skills in Berry and Mushroom Foraging ensure I can identify and gather them effectively while considering future availability. I will only collect a modest amount to satiate my hunger without impacting the berry patches significantly, maintaining a cautious balance with the environment. I will avoid hunting deer or rabbits today to preserve wildlife patterns and maintain ecological balance.\n\nFinally, I will observe the wildlife, particularly the deer and foxes, to monitor any changes in their behavior in response to my actions. This will inform future strategies for sustainable coexistence.\n\nOverall, my actions will focus on fulfilling immediate needs while reinforcing my commitment to sustainable resource management and ecological mindfulness."
}

